+## Idle loops
+
+`[idle]` names the head block of a guest wait loop. The translator emits an `idle_poll` call at the
+start of that block; the runtime compares two consecutive turns and, when nothing happened between
+them (no interrupt, trap or device access, same registers except the cycle count and the loop
+counter), adds the cycles of the turns that cannot reach the next scheduler event instead of running
+them. The turn that reaches the event runs as translated, so interrupts land on the same cycle as
+without skipping. `--no-idle-skip` on the launcher turns it off; the report counts the skips.
+
+Kinds:
+
+- `katana_wait_vblank`: the inner loop of Katana's `kmWaitVBlank`. `@r15` points at a timeout word
+  that each turn lowers by one, and `r3` holds it at the loop head; the skip lowers it by the number
+  of turns skipped.
+
 ## What `dream-translate game` does
 
 ```sh
